	(text "The \"Under-Resistor\" Routing Strategy\nSince you are using a 2-terminal resistor like the Bourns CRA2512,\nfollow these specific steps for the \"Under-Resistor\" method:\nThe Entry Points: Bring your 8A power traces into the outer ends \nof the pads. This ensures the high-current \"highway\" doesn't \noverlap with your sensing \"sidewalk.\"\nThe Sense Taps: Start your CSP and CSN traces from the inner edge\nof the pads.\nThe Underpass: Immediately dive those two thin traces (6-8 mil) \ninto the empty space directly beneath the resistor body (between \nthe two pads).\nDifferential Pairing: Once they are under the resistor, snap them\ntogether as a differential pair. Keep the gap between them as \nsmall as your PCB manufacturer allows (typically 6 mil).\nThe Exit: Route them out from under the resistor together, heading \nstraight for the LTC4020 sense pins."
